        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(stt-live-audio): drain ElevenLabs error response body to release socket",
        "body": "## Problem\n\n`synthesizeElevenLabsLiveSpeech` in `src/plugin-sdk/test-helpers/stt-live-audio.ts` already had an `AbortController` deadline, but on a non-2xx response it threw without consuming or cancelling the response body. On keep-alive HTTP connections the unread error body holds the socket open, leaking connection slots in live STT test runs that hit 4xx/5xx from ElevenLabs.\n\n## Fix\n\nDrain the error body via `response.arrayBuffer()` (with a `response.body?.cancel()` fallback) before throwing so the underlying connection is released back to the pool.\n\n## Real HTTP keep-alive proof\n\nA new test `releases the real keep-alive socket after a non-2xx error response` starts a local HTTP server that returns a streaming 401 response with keep-alive (64KB chunks every 50ms, timeout=30s). The helper is called with `ELEVENLABS_BASE_URL` pointed at the local server. After the call throws:\n\n- **With fix:** `arrayBuffer()` drains the error body → socket closes → `activeConnections` drops to 0\n- **Without fix:** The unread streaming error body keeps the socket open → `activeConnections` stays at 1 (leaked)\n\n```\n ✓ |extension-media| ../../extensions/elevenlabs/tts.test.ts (17 tests) 2693ms\n     ✓ releases the real keep-alive socket after a non-2xx error response  2521ms\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  17 passed (17)\n```\n\nThe mock-based test `drains the error response body when ElevenLabs returns non-2xx` also asserts `arrayBuffer` is called on the error response.\n\n## Risk",
        "branch": "fix/stt-live-audio-body-cancel",
